      "en": "### Useful EASTIE Spaces\n\nClassroom  \nSmall outdoor grass area attached to PG classroom  \nCircle-time area / mat area  \nTable activity area  \nBook corner  \nToy shelf / classroom storage area  \nLego area  \nConstruction / block room  \nSmall theatre or movement space\n\n### Useful Materials\n\nName cards  \nTeacher puppet  \nClass mascot  \nSoft toys  \nClassroom object cards  \nReal classroom objects  \nBags  \nCups  \nBooks  \nToy baskets  \nClean-up boxes  \nMats  \nChairs  \nSmall blocks  \nLego bricks  \nLarge wooden blocks  \nScarves  \nSimple rhythm instruments  \nVisual routine cards\n\n### Enhanced Resource Opportunities\n\nA class mascot can be used across the unit to model greeting, sitting, listening, cleaning up, and saying bye-bye. Personal objects such as bags, cups, and name cards can help children connect classroom participation with their own identity and belongings. Classroom storage spaces can be turned into “object homes” so that clean-up becomes a meaningful game rather than a mechanical task.",
